## Known Traps

| Trap | Why it matters | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| G1 asset no longer exists | Previous `/Game/_MCP_Temp/ReactiveGhost/` was cleaned, so T7-T10 must recreate the source-template clone. | Use the runner's `promote_niagara_system_candidate` steps. |
| Editor-world tick/readback is not runtime proof | Earlier G1 needed SIE game-world spawn for trusted write evidence. | T10 refuses to pass if readback world is `editor_world`. |
| T8 cannot pass from RT readback alone | Material consumer can flip V even when RT samples are correct. | Require PIE viewport capture and pixel-coordinate comparison. |
| Raw `AssetImportTask` PNG import crashed in V3 | UE 5.6.1 Interchange recursion guard crash was observed. | Use guarded importer paths only; this T7-T11 runner does not import textures. |
| RT UAV property name differs by Python exposure | `supports_uav` may not be the exact Python property name. | Script tries multiple property names and records which one worked. |
| `advance_simulation` may not be exposed | Without a deterministic tick route, Niagara readback can be stale. | Script falls back to `tick_component`; otherwise test is BLOCKED. |
| GPU timing may not be numerically readable from Python | `stat gpu` can be sent but not parsed as a number through this route. | Record command-sent status separately from RT/User-param proof. |
| T9 signatures are not unique yet | Three identical G1 stamps prove independent RT writes but not perfect cross-talk isolation. | Follow-up should add distinct color/channel signatures per system. |
| T11 is not a smoke | Runtime resize support would expand test surface substantially. | Treat BeginPlay fixed sizing as the Phase 0-2 decision unless user rejects it. |

